<!doctype html><html><head><title>SECURITY.md</title></head><body><div id="app"><aside>menu</aside><article><h1>Security Policy</h1>
<h2>Supported versions</h2>
<p>Only the latest release of Mixdog receives security fixes. Update before
reporting, and check whether the problem still occurs.</p>
<h2>Reporting a vulnerability</h2>
<p><strong>Do not report vulnerabilities in public issues, discussions, or pull requests.</strong></p>
<p>Report privately through
<a href="https://github.com/tribgames/mixdog/security/advisories/new">GitHub private vulnerability reporting</a>.
Include:</p>
<ul>
<li>What an attacker can do, and what they need first (local access, a crafted
file, a malicious website, a signed-in account).</li>
<li>Steps to reproduce or a proof of concept, against the latest release.</li>
<li>The affected version and operating system.</li>
</ul>
<p>Keep the details private until a fix is released. We credit reporters in the
release notes unless you ask us not to.</p>
<h2>Out of scope</h2>
<ul>
<li>A dependency with a known CVE, without showing that Mixdog actually reaches
the vulnerable code.</li>
<li>Actions that need the user to run commands or approve tools they were warned
about.</li>
<li>Problems in third-party model providers or MCP servers themselves.</li>
</ul>
</article></div></body></html>